## Phase 1 — Tape-only factors (no model fitting)

Each prompt: implement, unit-test against hand-computed toy examples, then smoke-run on one liquid and one illiquid synthetic bond and plot the factor path.

### P1.1 — Signed-flow family (F1, F2, F3, F5)
> Using the compendium definitions, implement in `factors/flow.py`: F1 last-trade sign with time-since-trade attached; F2 signed-spread interaction in both forms (use realized effective spread from F22 as the spread proxy when quotes are absent); F3 exponentially decayed signed flow F_t(β) for the half-life grid {1,5,21}d, normalized by amount outstanding — implement the O(1) recursive update F ← F·exp(−βΔt) + d·V/AmtOut, not a rolling sum; F5 per-side VWAPs, their gap G_t, and volume pressure Π_t. Hand-check: a tape of 3 prints with known times must reproduce F3 to 1e-12 against the closed form.

### P1.2 — Reversal / pressure family (F9, F10, F11, F12, F14)
> Implement `factors/reversal.py`: F9 EMA- and VWAP-deviation reversal; F10 volume-conditioned reversal (both forms; CsRank strictly within rating×maturity×sector buckets from P0.4); F11 range position K_t(n) and its rank-fade; F12 the IfElse dislocation switch with threshold c set to 0.5 × trailing median effective spread; F14 all three price–volume divergence forms. All ranks must handle ties and missing bonds gracefully (rank among non-missing, propagate NaN otherwise). Positive control: on synthetic data, F10 must show a significantly positive 5-day IC because reversal-after-volume is planted.

### P1.3 — Liquidity family (F19, F20, F21, F22, F24)
> Implement `factors/liquidity.py`: F19 Amihud on daily aggregates; F20 resilience delta exactly as specified (guard ε in the denominator); F21 amount efficiency + velocity + acceleration on turnover = volume/AmtOut; F22 realized effective spread from F5's per-side VWAPs at δ ∈ {5, 21} days; F24 quote-update intensity IF quote data exists, else emit NaN with a logged warning, never zeros. Then orthogonalize F21 against F19 cross-sectionally (residual of bucket-wise regression) and store both raw and orthogonalized versions.

### P1.4 — Momentum family (F25, F26, F27)
> Implement `factors/momentum.py`: F25 studentized momentum on both price and (if OAS available) spread changes; F26 trend-reliability — rolling OLS of log price on time per bond over 21/63-day windows, output sgn(slope)·R² and the double-rank form; F27 both lead–lag rank forms using first/last prints per bar from P0.5. Efficiency requirement: the rolling regressions must be vectorized (running sums for slope and R², no per-window OLS refits). Cross-check the running-sum R² against statsmodels on 100 random windows.

### P1.5 — Volatility family (F28, F29, F30)
> Implement `factors/volatility.py`: F28 realized vol (with the range-based fallback R/Q50 from P0.6 when there are <5 prints in the window), the inverse-vol tilt, and vol-amplified reversal; F29 vol-of-vol; F30 rolling skew/kurt on 63-day windows with shrinkage toward the bucket mean (shrinkage weight ∝ n/(n+n₀), pick n₀=60), plus the kurtosis regime switch. Document in comments why raw 21-day skew on a sparse tape is unusable (show the standard error).

### P1.6 — Composite mined expressions (§12)
> Implement the six translated mined expressions X(1)…X(6) from §12 of the compendium in `factors/mined.py`, reusing K_t, R_t, VWAP deviation, and rank utilities from earlier modules — no duplicated logic. Add a redundancy check: report the pairwise Spearman correlation of X(1)…X(6) with the Phase-1 factors they were derived from, and flag any pair >0.9 as expected-duplicate.

