## Phase 3 — Estimated factors (models fitted, strictly walk-forward)

### P3.1 — Hawkes states (F4)
> Implement `estimation/hawkes.py`: fit univariate exponential Hawkes (μ, α, β) per flow type (customer buy / customer sell) by MLE, pooled within liquidity bucket per Algorithm 2's pooling logic — parameters per bucket, states per bond. Use the standard recursive log-likelihood; verify the estimator on simulated Hawkes data (recover parameters within 10% at n=5000 events). Then emit F4 states H_i(t) = log(μ + decayed sum) per bond, computed with the same O(1) recursion as F3. Refit quarterly, walk-forward only.

### P3.2 — Impact state (F13, Algorithm 2)
> Implement Algorithm 2 steps 3–4 in `estimation/impact.py`: for each liquidity bucket, regress future h-day returns (h ∈ {1,5,21}) on F_t(β) for each β in the half-life grid, all walk-forward with an expanding window and a 21-day embargo; select β by out-of-sample R²; back out λ from the slope rescaled by (1−e^{−βh}); emit F13 = −λ·F_t(β*) and the de-pressured price. Report the selected half-life per bucket — on synthetic data it must approximately recover the planted impact decay.

### P3.3 — Toxicity propensity (F31, F32, F34, Algorithm 3)
> Implement Algorithm 3 in `estimation/toxicity.py`. Markout horizon G ∈ {1, 5} days against the F15 fair value, threshold c = 0.5 × trailing effective spread. Feature grid exactly as F31 specifies: the eight statistics × three clocks × nested horizons, level features, signed-log transforms; since public TRACE has no client IDs, substitute trade-size buckets and side-persistence features and note this. Classifier: gradient boosting with isotonic calibration, walk-forward with embargo ≥ G. Emit: per-print propensity, F31 toxicity-weighted signed flow over trailing {5,21}d, and F34's informed/uninformed decomposition Q^I, Q^U with their rank factors. Evaluate the classifier itself first (AUC, calibration curve, feature importance by clock) before building the factors.

### P3.4 — VPIN (F33)
> Implement `factors/vpin.py`: volume buckets of size V* = 1/50 of trailing 21-day volume per bond, VPIN over N=50 buckets, using TRACE side flags directly (no bulk classification needed). Then test its designed role: does high VPIN predict (a) next-period realized vol and (b) the *conditional profitability of F10* (interaction regression), rather than direction? Report both.

### P3.5 — Intensity ratios (F35, F36, Algorithm 4)
> Implement Algorithm 4 in `estimation/intensity_ratio.py`: logistic regression of next-event side on covariates {Π_t, F1, F2 (both forms), F4 states, F3 fast} sampled at event times, pooled within buckets, walk-forward. Model selection by BIC over the covariate power set up to size 5 (or L1 path if that's cleaner) — report which sets win and check the compendium's two predictions: imbalance-alone loses; the s·ε interaction survives. Emit F35 = 2p̂−1 continuously. Then F36: second-stage logistic for aggressiveness (print at/through the far composite quote if quotes exist; else within the top/bottom decile of the day's print range as proxy) and the combined directional factor.

### P3.6 — State-conditional tables (F23, F37, Algorithm 6)
> Implement Algorithm 6 in `estimation/state_tables.py`: state = (effective-spread tercile, log-staleness bucket ×4, last-flow sign), pooled within liquidity buckets; accumulate the four conditional estimates in one pass with running sums; k-NN smoothing over adjacent cells with opposite-sign cells infinitely distant; two-stage prediction output. Also emit F23 = Ê[τ|S] as a standalone factor and as the tradability gate: a boolean `tradable_h` per bond-day-horizon, h < Ê[τ|S] ⇒ False. Minimum cell count 200; report the fraction of state space that meets it.

### P3.7 — Sparse fair-value selection (Algorithm 5)
> Implement Algorithm 5 in `estimation/fv_selection.py`: the full grid from P0.6 (a few hundred candidates, per side, per horizon, with realized-horizon columns), standardized within date×bucket; LASSO of h-day forward returns with penalty by walk-forward validation; importance = summed |coef| grouped by (feature type, horizon, side). Deliverable: a table + bar chart of grouped importance. Test the compendium's prior: percentiles/min/max at medium horizons should dominate and volume features should drop — flag if they don't and investigate before proceeding.

