## Phase 5 — Wrap-up

### P5.1 — Reproducibility audit
> Audit the whole pipeline for lookahead: list every place a factor at time t could touch data after t (label construction, normalizations fitted on full sample, bucket definitions, rank pools, model refits) and either prove each is walk-forward or fix it. Then produce `REPORT.md`: per-family results table, the pool composition, the transfer-test result, and the synthetic-data positive/placebo control outcomes.

### P5.2 — Real-data rerun (when subscriptions available)
> Swap the loader from synthetic to WRDS data from MarketDB (P0.2 option 1), rerun `make clean-data bars factors evaluate` end-to-end, and produce a diff report: which factors that worked on synthetic data survive on real data at |IC t| > 2, which die, and whether the F10 / F13 / F25 family — the ones with documented real-world credit evidence — behave as the literature predicts.

